SUMMARY:City Commission Conference Mtg — Alridge Post Office Site (CAM #26-0409)
LOCATION:City Hall "101 Building"\, 100 N. Andrews Avenue\, 11th Floor Conference Room\, Fort Lauderdale\, FL
DESCRIPTION:Fort Lauderdale City Commission Conference Meeting — Consideration of the Future Use of the USPS Alridge Station Post Office site\, 400 NW 7th Avenue (CAM #26-0409\, District 2).\n\nTime: Fran (BPHI) says 1:00 PM\; City's posted Conference Meeting start is 1:30 PM — arriving at 1:00 covers both.\n\nWhy it matters: City weighing options incl. conveyance to CRA/Housing Authority for affordable housing (≤80% AMI)\, surplus sale (May 2026 appraisal: $13.5M)\, or RFP under F.S. 255.065. This is the Heritage Crossing site.\n\nWho: Dodie + Margi Nothard attending for the Partnership. Fran and Debbie cannot attend.\n\nBefore the meeting: call/email Mayor Trantalis (954-828-5314\, dtrantalis@fortlauderdale.gov) re: BPHI interest + federal funding experience (Dodie's ask via Fran\, 6/12). Debbie calling Herbst\; Dodie calling Sorensen and Glassman.\n\nMaterials: Commission Agenda Memo 26-0409 + USPS Site Presentation (attached to Fran's 6/12 email).
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Commission meeting in 1 hour — head to 100 N. Andrews Ave
TRIGGER:-PT1H
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
